jobs.description:
Do you enjoy coordinating logistics processes and working with different stakeholders? Join Syngenta as a Logistics & Supply Specialist and help ensure products are delivered on time and efficiently.

What are you going to do?
- Manage customer orders, shipments, and logistics activities;
- Coordinate transport and logistics providers;
- Process orders and shipment data in SAP;
- Monitor deliveries and resolve supply chain issues;
- Work closely with customers, suppliers, and internal teams;
- Support process improvements and logistics optimization.

What do we offer?
- Gross hourly salary of €21.50;
- Part-time position for 15 hours per week;
- Temporary contract from 4 January 2027 until 31 May 2027;
- Based in Enkhuizen, working 2 days per week (3 days negotiable);
- Opportunity to work in an international and innovative organization;
- Dynamic role with extensive stakeholder interaction;
- 25 vacation days per year based on full-time employment;
- 8.33% holiday allowance;
- Pension scheme from your first day of employment;
- Access to the Adecco Academy for personal and professional development.

Where will you work?
Join a global leader in agricultural innovation, helping growers produce stronger and more resilient crops. You'll work in an international, diverse, and collaborative environment focused on solving global food production challenges.

What do we ask?
- HBO/Bachelor degree in Logistics, Supply Chain, Business Administration, or similar;
- Experience in logistics, customer service, supply chain, or order management;
- SAP experience is a strong plus;
- Strong organizational and communication skills;
- Ability to work independently while also being a team player;
- Proactive mindset with a focus on finding practical solutions;
- Comfortable interacting with multiple departments and external stakeholders;
- Fluent in English (Dutch is a plus).

Are you interested?
Interested? Apply now and become part of the international spply chain team! Questions?

